lisa-design:
- SUPERSEDES the alpine/apk/jq design (chart owner decision, 2026-10-06): the bootstrap Job runs on curlimages/curl:8.22.0 as uid 100/gid 101 (numeric, because the image USER is the name curl_user and kubelet cannot verify runAsNonRoot against a name), read-only root FS, /tmp emptyDir, nothing installed at runtime. The pod passes Pod Security "restricted" (server dry-run, no warnings).
- No jq: request JSON is built by curl --expand-data with {{VAR:json}} / {{VAR:b64}} (curl >= 8.3), values via --variable %ENV or NAME@file, so no secret is in argv and no shell escaping is needed. Responses are read by grep/sed on single known keys whose values have known charsets in api v0.21.0: auth_token RS256 JWT [A-Za-z0-9_.-]; ids/client-ids lowercase UUID; client-secret base64.RawURLEncoding(32B) [A-Za-z0-9_-]{43}. encoding/json escapes every '"' inside strings, so "key": patterns only match real keys.
- Agent lookup: GET /api/admin/agents has no name filter and POST accepts duplicate names, so the script matches the "id","created-at","updated-at","name" field sequence (agentResponse struct order). Agent names are restricted to [A-Za-z0-9 ._-] (start/end alnum) so the JSON form equals the raw name; '.' is escaped for the BRE. Descriptions stay free text (BOOTSTRAP_AGENT_<i>_DESCRIPTION, JSON-encoded by curl).
- The script lives in files/agent-bootstrap.sh and is included with .Files.Get, so curl's {{...}} templates are not parsed by Helm and the file can be shellchecked directly.
